   577→### Pattern 5: Program Selector Component
   578→
   579→**What:** Dropdown selector to switch between pre-scripted programs
   580→
   581→**When to use:** For DEMO-06 and DEMO-07 requirements - allow switching between programs
   582→
   583→**Example:**
   584→```javascript
   585→// Pattern: Program selector with auto-load
   586→// Source: Standard <select> dropdown pattern
   587→
   588→class ProgramSelector {
   589→  constructor(container, engine, visualizer, instructionList) {
   590→    this.container = container;
   591→    this.engine = engine;
   592→    this.visualizer = visualizer;
   593→    this.instructionList = instructionList;
   594→
   595→    // Available programs (from Phase 9)
   596→    this.programs = {
   597→      basic: BASIC_PROGRAM,
   598→      fibonacci: FIBONACCI_PROGRAM
   599→    };
   600→
   601→    this.currentProgramKey = 'basic';
   602→
   603→    this._createSelector();
   604→    this._loadProgram(this.currentProgramKey);
   605→  }
   606→
   607→  _createSelector() {
   608→    this.container.innerHTML = `
   609→      <label for="program-select">Select Program:</label>
   610→      <select id="program-select" aria-label="Program selector">
   611→        <option value="basic">Basic Instructions Walkthrough</option>
   612→        <option value="fibonacci">Fibonacci Sequence</option>
   613→      </select>
   614→    `;
   615→
   616→    this.selectElement = this.container.querySelector('#program-select');
   617→    this.selectElement.addEventListener('change', (e) => {
   618→      this.currentProgramKey = e.target.value;
   619→      this._loadProgram(this.currentProgramKey);
   620→    });
   621→  }
   622→
   623→  _loadProgram(programKey) {
   624→    const program = this.programs[programKey];
   625→
   626→    // Generate frame sequence
   627→    const result = SequenceGenerator.generateSequence(program.instructions);
   628→
   629→    // Load frames into animation engine
   630→    this.engine.loadFrames(result.frames);
   631→
   632→    // Update instruction list if available
   633→    if (this.instructionList) {
   634→      this.instructionList.loadProgram(program, result);
   635→    }
   636→
   637→    // Trigger initial render
   638→    this.visualizer.render(result.frames[0]);
   639→  }
   640→}
   641→```
   642→
   643→**Why this pattern:**
   644→- Simple `<select>` dropdown (no custom UI library needed)
   645→- Auto-loads and resets animation when program changes
   646→- Updates instruction list to show new program
   647→- Programs already defined in Phase 9 (BASIC_PROGRAM, FIBONACCI_PROGRAM)
   648→
   649→## Don't Hand-Roll
   650→
   651→| Problem | Don't Build | Use Instead | Why |
   652→|---------|-------------|-------------|-----|
   653→| Animation timing | Custom setInterval-based playback | requestAnimationFrame with AnimationEngine | Already built in Phase 9 - handles visibility, delta-time, speed control |
   654→| State management | Redux/MobX state library | AnimationEngine frame array | Overkill for pre-scripted sequences - frames are already immutable snapshots |
   655→| Keyboard shortcuts | Custom key detection logic | Standard event.code checks | Native API sufficient - no library needed for simple shortcuts |
   656→| Hex formatting | Custom padding/conversion | toString(16).padStart(8, '0') | Native methods handle hex conversion correctly |
   657→| Table virtualization | React-virtualized or similar | Native `<table>` with filtered rows | Only ~256 memory addresses, most zeros - filter non-zero addresses instead |
   658→
   659→**Key insight:** Most infrastructure already exists from Phase 9 and 10. This phase is primarily UI wiring, not new algorithms.
   660→
   661→## Common Pitfalls
   662→
   663→### Pitfall 1: Instruction-to-Frame Mapping Errors
   664→
   665→**What goes wrong:** Clicking instruction jumps to wrong frame because each instruction spans 5 frames (IF, ID, EX, MEM, WB)
   666→
   667→**Why it happens:** Naive calculation (instruction index * 5) fails for branches/jumps that change PC non-linearly
   668→
   669→**How to avoid:** Build instruction-to-frame map by scanning frame sequence and recording first IF stage frame for each PC value
   670→
   671→**Warning signs:** Clicking instruction 3 shows instruction 2 executing; branch instructions jump to wrong targets
   672→
   673→**Solution:**
   674→```javascript
   675→// Build map from PC to frame index
   676→const pcToFrame = new Map();
   677→frameSequence.frames.forEach((frame, index) => {
   678→  if (frame.pipeline.IF.active) {
   679→    const pc = frame.pipeline.IF.pc;
   680→    if (!pcToFrame.has(pc)) {
   681→      pcToFrame.set(pc, index);
   682→    }
   683→  }
   684→});
   685→```
   686→
   687→### Pitfall 2: Button State Sync Issues
   688→
   689→**What goes wrong:** Step forward/backward buttons remain enabled when at boundaries, or play/pause button shows wrong icon
   690→
   691→**Why it happens:** Button states not updated after AnimationEngine state changes (play/pause/step)
   692→
   693→**How to avoid:** Listen to cpu:framechange events and update button states in response; use engine.isAtStart() and engine.isAtEnd() checks
   694→
   695→**Warning signs:** Clicking "Step Forward" at last frame does nothing but button still enabled; "Play" button shows "Play" even when playing
   696→
   697→**Solution:**
   698→```javascript
   699→window.addEventListener('cpu:framechange', () => {
   700→  btnStepBack.disabled = engine.isAtStart();
   701→  btnStepForward.disabled = engine.isAtEnd();
   702→  btnPlayPause.textContent = engine.isPlaying ? 'Pause' : 'Play';
   703→});
   704→```
   705→
   706→### Pitfall 3: Memory View Performance with 256 Rows
   707→
   708→**What goes wrong:** Rendering all 256 memory addresses (even zeros) causes slow DOM updates
   709→
   710→**Why it happens:** Most memory addresses are zero throughout execution - rendering all rows is wasteful
   711→
   712→**How to avoid:** Filter memory array to show only non-zero addresses; show "No memory in use" message when all zero
   713→
   714→**Warning signs:** Memory view renders slowly (>100ms); scrolling feels janky; DevTools Performance shows long DOM layout times
   715→
   716→**Solution:**
   717→```javascript
   718→// Only render non-zero memory addresses
   719→const activeAddresses = [];
   720→for (let i = 0; i < state.memory.length; i++) {
   721→  if (state.memory[i] !== 0) {
   722→    activeAddresses.push(i);
   723→  }
   724→}
   725→// Render only activeAddresses.length rows instead of 256
   726→```
   727→
   728→### Pitfall 4: Keyboard Shortcuts Conflict with Browser Shortcuts
   729→
   730→**What goes wrong:** Pressing Space scrolls page instead of play/pause; Arrow keys scroll instead of step
   731→
   732→**Why it happens:** Browser default actions not prevented for keyboard shortcut keys
   733→
   734→**How to avoid:** Call `event.preventDefault()` for all keyboard shortcut handlers; check `e.target === document.body` to avoid triggering when typing in inputs
   735→
   736→**Warning signs:** Space bar scrolls page; Arrow keys scroll instead of stepping; shortcuts work inconsistently
   737→
   738→**Solution:**
   739→```javascript
   740→document.addEventListener('keydown', (e) => {
   741→  // Only handle shortcuts when not in input field
   742→  if (e.target.tagName === 'INPUT' || e.target.tagName === 'TEXTAREA') {
   743→    return;
   744→  }
   745→
   746→  if (e.code === 'Space') {
   747→    e.preventDefault(); // Prevent page scroll
   748→    engine.togglePlayPause();
   749→  }
   750→});
   751→```
   752→
   753→### Pitfall 5: Current Instruction Display Shows Wrong Stage
   754→
   755→**What goes wrong:** Instruction view shows NOP when instruction is actually in MEM or WB stage
   756→
   757→**Why it happens:** Phase 10 decision uses state.pipeline.IF.instruction for all stages (non-pipelined mode), but InstructionView checks wrong stage
   758→
   759→**How to avoid:** Follow Phase 10 pattern - always read state.pipeline.IF.instruction regardless of which stage is active; check activeStages to determine display
   760→
   761→**Warning signs:** Instruction view shows nothing even though BlockDiagramView shows active instruction; instruction display lags behind animation
   762→
   763→**Solution:**
   764→```javascript
   765→// CORRECT: Check which stage is active, but always read IF.instruction
   766→let currentInstruction = null;
   767→if (state.activeStages.size > 0 && state.pipeline.IF.instruction) {
   768→  currentInstruction = state.pipeline.IF.instruction;
   769→
   770→  // Determine which stage for display label
   771→  if (state.pipeline.WB.active) stageName = 'WB';
   772→  else if (state.pipeline.MEM.active) stageName = 'MEM';
   773→  // ... etc
   774→}
   775→```
